    "narrative": "For Ghost Ride the WHIP today, the clear catalyst is **Corbin Carroll**, who leads the board with an elite 87.14 efficiency score. The combination of his high-leverage spot in the two-hole against Lorenzen and a massive 14% park factor boost makes him our primary anchor. We are also leaning heavily into **James Wood** (78.42) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (76.91); **James Wood** capitalizes on his lead-off role and high xwOBA against a vulnerable Young, while **Tyler Soderstrom** draws a plus-matchup against Houser that allows him to exploit the park factors and SP skill metrics. **Vinnie Pasquantino** (76.21) remains an essential play, as the combination of a platoon advantage and an \"Out\" wind factor provides enough ceiling to offset a slight park penalty.\n\nOur lineup construction emphasizes aggressive base-running opportunities, specifically with **Brice Turang** and **Seiya Suzuki**. **Brice Turang** (68.77) benefits from Ober\u2019s slow delivery, which projects to boost his stolen base probability, while **Seiya Suzuki** (65.87) similarly exploits a matchup against Fedde where the pitcher\u2019s tempo provides a subtle boost to his utility. On the fringe, **Kyle Karros** (45.40) was the most difficult exclusion from the starting nine; while his park factor in the Soroka matchup is significant, his low spot in the batting order ultimately pushed his score below the threshold required to displace our current starters. We are monitoring **Brice Turang** closely, as the \"Wind In\" warning could dampen the power potential of our secondary hitters, though the platoon edge remains firm. Meanwhile, we continue to carry **Jose Caballero** and **Giancarlo Stanton** on the bench in hopes of near-term returns from the IL, keeping our daily cap management tight.",
